            <description><![CDATA[<p class="jarvis-headline">Tasks you finish stay finished.</p>
<h2>Jarvis 0.20.36</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Jarvis no longer makes a second copy of a task you already have, so a task you mark done won’t seem to come back the next day.</li>
  <li>Reading a meeting again, for example after renaming a speaker, adds to the tasks it already gave you instead of creating new ones.</li>
  <li>When someone chases a request in Slack, the existing task is updated rather than duplicated.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
